<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Büdingen</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Büdingen is a town in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wetterau">Wetterau</a> district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hesse">Hesse</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, known for its well-preserved medieval walls and old town. Its moated castle was the seat of the counts of Isenburg-Büdingen, who in the 18th century allowed religious dissenters, among them the Inspirationists and Moravians, to settle on nearby estates. The princely family of Ysenburg and Büdingen still owns the castle.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/budingen.jpg" alt="Büdingen" width="320" height="190" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jörg Braukmann · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:B%C3%BCdingen-Altstadt_(Wilder_Stein).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
